WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.388
Across an organisation, every new tool promises speed.

2
00:00:03.388 --> 00:00:06.775
Then URLs multiply, permissions diverge, bookmarks go stale,

3
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:10.161
and IT keeps answering the same question: where

4
00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:12.702
do I find the right app?

5
00:00:13.115 --> 00:00:16.475
Frontdoor creates one clear way in: simple for

6
00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:19.415
people, governable for the teams running IT.

7
00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:25.669
This is Meridian Works’ catalogue: sixteen business applications,

8
00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:29.624
organised and described, with owners, tags, and access

9
00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:32.095
modes visible at a glance.

10
00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:37.450
Search for security, and Frontdoor brings the relevant

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:41.086
tools forward instantly, without asking anyone to remember

12
00:00:41.086 --> 00:00:42.905
product names or URLs.

13
00:00:44.165 --> 00:00:47.415
Tags turn the catalogue into a readable map.

14
00:00:47.415 --> 00:00:50.665
With favourites, personal ordering, and a compact view,

15
00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:53.915
each person can shape their own starting point.

16
00:00:54.515 --> 00:00:57.890
Move from the complete catalogue to everyday apps

17
00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.265
in seconds. The complexity stays behind the door.

18
00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:06.791
Behind that simplicity is operational control. Administrators manage

19
00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:10.718
applications, status, order, and visibility from one console,

20
00:01:10.718 --> 00:01:14.154
without chasing spreadsheets or stale wiki pages.

21
00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.550
Each record brings together its name, description, icon,

22
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.510
destination, groups, and tags. The configuration is explicit:

23
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:26.470
what users see always follows a precise rule.

24
00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:30.742
Users and groups determine who sees what. Technology,

25
00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:34.602
operations, finance, or leadership: Frontdoor assembles a relevant

26
00:01:34.602 --> 00:01:38.462
catalogue for each group while keeping governance central.

27
00:01:40.108 --> 00:01:43.176
Here, local groups coexist with groups from the

28
00:01:43.176 --> 00:01:46.246
directory. Membership and assigned applications are visible in

29
00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:47.398
the same place.

30
00:01:49.958 --> 00:01:54.180
Distinct roles separate management, read-only administration, and everyday

31
00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.404
use, keeping administrative access proportional to each person’s

32
00:01:58.404 --> 00:01:58.931
responsibilities.

33
00:01:59.308 --> 00:02:02.868
Elena, the IT owner, sees sixteen applications. Luca,

34
00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:06.428
a standard user, sees seven: only those assigned

35
00:02:06.428 --> 00:02:09.988
through his groups. One door, relevant for each.

36
00:02:10.658 --> 00:02:14.138
Frontdoor does not impose one integration model. It

37
00:02:14.138 --> 00:02:17.618
can open direct links, route through SSO, reach

38
00:02:17.618 --> 00:02:21.098
internal resources, reuse a shared session, or delegate

39
00:02:21.098 --> 00:02:22.838
authentication to Microsoft Entra.

40
00:02:26.008 --> 00:02:28.925
The outcome is tangible: one click on Signal

41
00:02:28.925 --> 00:02:31.844
Ops opens the right operational dashboard. Frontdoor is

42
00:02:31.844 --> 00:02:34.762
the entry point; the application keeps doing its

43
00:02:34.762 --> 00:02:35.128
job.

44
00:02:35.858 --> 00:02:39.811
Frontdoor records access events with user, application, time,

45
00:02:39.811 --> 00:02:43.765
and context. IT can understand real usage and

46
00:02:43.765 --> 00:02:45.248
investigate issues faster.

47
00:02:46.582 --> 00:02:50.019
The audit log also tells the story of

48
00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:53.455
administrative changes: not only where people enter, but

49
00:02:53.455 --> 00:02:56.032
how the configuration changes over time.

50
00:02:56.432 --> 00:03:00.498
Logo, messages, language, theme, and home behaviour are

51
00:03:00.498 --> 00:03:04.564
configurable. Frontdoor adapts to the organisation without losing

52
00:03:04.564 --> 00:03:05.072
consistency.

53
00:03:06.282 --> 00:03:09.042
Frontdoor is open source and self-hosted. It starts

54
00:03:09.042 --> 00:03:11.802
with Docker, keeps data and configuration in your

55
00:03:11.802 --> 00:03:14.562
environment, and leaves IT in control of the

56
00:03:14.562 --> 00:03:15.252
entry point.

57
00:03:19.508 --> 00:03:22.814
Less time searching. Fewer disconnected access points. One

58
00:03:22.814 --> 00:03:26.120
door for the applications that keep the business

59
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:26.948
running. Frontdoor.
